<Folder><name>Our hotel</name>
<Placemark><name>Bruce Bowker&#x27;s Carib Inn</name><description>Address: J.A. Abraham Blvd 46, Kralendijk
Our hotel. Small waterfront dive inn with an on-site PADI 5-Star dive center; daily boat trips 8:30 and 1:30 to north/south sites and Klein Bonaire. House reef/shore entry not confirmed on the official site, so ask at check-in.
Source: OSM way 371233370 (hotel, J.A. Abraham Blvd); matches bonaire.com 12.14228,-68.27556; address from caribinn.com
https://caribinn.com/</description><styleUrl>#hotel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.27549,12.14227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Shore dive</name>
<Placemark><name>1000 Steps</name><description>Skill: All levels
Depth: 20–100 ft
Easy water entry but a tough climb out of ~67 steps.
Source: OSM way 1495901720 (BNMP #16); matches bonaire.com 12.2108,-68.3216</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.32187,12.21087,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Salt Pier</name><description>Skill: Beginner–intermediate
Depth: 13–60 ft
Closed when a salt ship is docked.
Source: OSM pier way 26326561; matches Diveity 12.0833,-68.2838 and bonaire.com 12.0828,-68.2836</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.2835,12.0834,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Karpata</name><description>Skill: Intermediate–advanced
Depth: 10–160 ft
Mornings only, skip in north wind; the wall is advanced.
Source: OSM node 663869440; matches bonaire.com 12.2195,-68.3521</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.35213,12.21929,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Andrea I</name><description>Skill: Easy / all levels
Depth: Varies – ask shop
Easy site and a good night dive.
Source: OSM node 663869426; matches bonaire.com 12.1882,-68.2970</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.29673,12.18841,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Andrea II</name><description>Skill: Easy / all levels
Depth: Varies – ask shop
Easy site and a good night dive.
Source: OSM node 636400643; matches bonaire.com 12.1913,-68.2980</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.29782,12.19136,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Oil Slick Leap</name><description>Skill: Easy–intermediate
Depth: 10–80 ft
Ladder or giant-stride entry; barracuda and turtles; easy night site.
Source: OSM node 663869425; matches bonaire.com 12.2002,-68.3086</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.30872,12.20017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Angel City</name><description>Skill: Intermediate
Depth: Varies – ask shop
Double reef; can run current.
Source: OSM node 663869415; matches bonaire.com 12.1034,-68.2872</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.28721,12.10339,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Alice in Wonderland</name><description>Skill: Intermediate
Depth: Varies – ask shop
Double reef; can run current.
Source: OSM node 635881804; matches Diveity 12.0992,-68.2862 (bonaire.com point rejected: it duplicates Hilma Hooker)</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.28529,12.0998,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bari Reef</name><description>Skill: Beginner
Depth: Varies – ask shop
House reef with very high fish diversity.
Source: OSM node 313862678 (BNMP #30); matches bonaire.com 12.1672,-68.2871</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.2872,12.16747,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Buddy&#x27;s Reef</name><description>Skill: Beginner
Depth: Varies – ask shop
Buddy Dive house reef with high fish diversity.
Source: OSM node 635094204; matches bonaire.com 12.1708,-68.2885</description><styleUrl>#shore</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.28882,12.17103,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Advanced</name>
<Placemark><name>Hilma Hooker (wreck)</name><description>Skill: Advanced
Depth: 60–110 ft
236-ft cargo wreck on sand between the Angel City reefs. Shore or boat (sources conflict), so confirm with your shop. Pin is the wreck; the shore marker is on the road just inland.
Source: OSM node 635881808; matches Diveity 12.1041,-68.2896 (bonaire.com 12.1051,-68.2885 = shore entry)</description><styleUrl>#advanced</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.29012,12.10375,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Boat only (Klein Bonaire)</name>
<Placemark><name>The Forest (Klein Bonaire)</name><description>Skill: Advanced
Depth: 25–100 ft
Deep black-coral slope on Klein&#x27;s southwest corner. Boat only.
Source: Diveity 12.1490,-68.3265; fits the SW corner of Klein on the OSM coastline (~70 m off). Approximate; bonaire.com point rejected (1 km offshore)</description><styleUrl>#boat</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.3265,12.149,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>No Name (Klein Bonaire)</name><description>Skill: Beginner–intermediate
Depth: Varies – ask shop
Reef off No Name Beach on Klein&#x27;s north shore. Boat or water taxi.
Source: bonaire.com 12.1687,-68.3052; sits just off No Name Beach (OSM beach way 317794966)</description><styleUrl>#boat</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.3052,12.1687,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Ebo&#x27;s Reef (Klein Bonaire)</name><description>Skill: Intermediate
Depth: Varies – ask shop
Known for big elephant-ear sponges. Boat only.
Source: bonaire.com 12.1684,-68.3137 (single source; ~90 m off Klein&#x27;s north coast on OSM)</description><styleUrl>#boat</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.3137,12.1684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Restricted (permit/guided)</name>
<Placemark><name>Town Pier</name><description>Skill: Guided only
Depth: Shallow
Shallow pillars with frogfish and seahorses. Night dive only, guided, with an operator permit.
Source: bonaire.com 12.1492,-68.2773; at OSM Town Pier way 320348590</description><styleUrl>#restricted</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-68.2773,12.1492,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
